From 559d8da5ec611c71edd9cafb54ca6e40dbebf5ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adedoyinjr <110180947+Adedoyinjr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:37:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(auction): encrypt name auction bid recovery material

Sealed-bid recovery secrets (salt, bid amount, deposit) are persisted so a committed
bid can be revealed later. They are now stored in an encrypted vault instead of
plaintext: PBKDF2 (SHA-256) derives the key from a passphrase and AES-GCM seals
the bids record. The passphrase, the derived key and the plaintext bids never
reach localStorage.

The recovery record is written and read back (decrypted and compared) before
the on-chain commit is signed or broadcast, so a storage failure can no longer
leave a user without the salt needed to reveal. A backup import refuses to
replace a non-empty vault without explicit confirmation and preserves the
current vault when validation or decryption fails.

Legacy plaintext records (both the zustand-persist and the versioned value
shapes) are detected and migrated into the encrypted vault, and are only removed
after the encrypted replacement is verified. The storage validation, the
cross-tab sync lifecycle and the contract id lookup that landed on develop keep
working with the encrypted layout.
